Description: Miscellaneous functions to facilitate data analysis projects. Descriptive tables report standardized mean differences (SMDs) by default when a grouping variable is supplied. For numeric and logical variables, SMDs are absolute pairwise differences in group means divided by the square root of the average within-group variances (Bernoulli variance is used for logical variables). For factors, SMDs are generalized Mahalanobis distances between group-specific multinomial proportions using the average multinomial covariance matrix; with more than two groups, the reported value is the mean of all pairwise SMDs. These calculations follow the unweighted implementation in the tableone package.
